ence/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "57a66f06ae49fb4197fc7dd298e5421c480bad9165b1e0e48371e7a5def4cfbf" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18282" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ac7cf98f9f7eaad6b9fdd30be032102f8ca59befb4a38c9a4d0f89d152fe5257" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "57a66f06ae49fb4197fc7dd298e5421c480bad9165b1e0e48371e7a5def4cfbf" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "57a66f06ae49fb4197fc7dd298e5421c480bad9165b1e0e48371e7a5def4cfbf" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "57a66f06ae49fb4197fc7dd298e5421c480bad9165b1e0e48371e7a5def4cfbf" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "57a66f06ae49fb4197fc7dd298e5421c480bad9165b1e0e48371e7a5def4cfbf" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "57a66f06ae49fb4197fc7dd298e5421c480bad9165b1e0e48371e7a5def4cfbf" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "57a66f06ae49fb4197fc7dd298e5421c480bad9165b1e0e48371e7a5def4cfbf" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18282" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "57a66f06ae49fb4197fc7dd298e5421c480bad9165b1e0e48371e7a5def4cfbf" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & k & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nequals $-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "57a66f06ae49fb4197fc7dd298e5421c480bad9165b1e0e48371e7a5def4cfbf" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & k & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ k & -2\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(1\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot k)+(0\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot 3)+(0\\cdot k-1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =2(k-2)+3-3 \\\\  & =2k-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}^{t}={c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-(-2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{23}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{c}_{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2k-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{23}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k-2} & =-1 \\\\ 1 & =-(k-2) \\\\ k-2 & =-1 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "57a66f06ae49fb4197fc7dd298e5421c480bad9165b1e0e48371e7a5def4cfbf" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319937" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ac7cf98f9f7eaad6b9fdd30be032102f8ca59befb4a38c9a4d0f89d152fe5257" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319937" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "57a66f06ae49fb4197fc7dd298e5421c480bad9165b1e0e48371e7a5def4cfbf" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319937" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "57a66f06ae49fb4197fc7dd298e5421c480bad9165b1e0e48371e7a5def4cfbf" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the entry ${a}_{22}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]$ if its determinant is $-16.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bdb35a4a91916c18bd3d9d00fa5be36c237dafd79d5fe92bc622d7d61b6eb23" "basis" 1131 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since we want the entry ${a}_{22}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{22}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{22} & =(-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{22}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{22}=\\frac{1}{-16}\\cdot 4=-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bdb35a4a91916c18bd3d9d00fa5be36c237dafd79d5fe92bc622d7d61b6eb23" "basis" 1131 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18284" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f90ed32d06641710e2d2ca7b996069a0ece3a9348e3bc6d82247d75ebaea841c" "basis" 1131 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18284" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bdb35a4a91916c18bd3d9d00fa5be36c237dafd79d5fe92bc622